From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3drm: progressive mesh edge collapse (3639)

d3drm: progressive mesh detail now removes faces. Detail (SetDetail,
SetFaceDetail, SetVertexDetail) was only stored; CreateMesh returned the full
mesh. The mesh is now reduced by edge collapse (shortest edge first, the far end
moves onto the near end, which goes to the middle; faces that degenerate are
dropped) until ceil(faces * detail) faces or ceil(vertices * detail) vertices
are left. CreateMesh and rendering (a progressive mesh added as a visual) use
the reduced mesh, cached until the detail or quality changes.
---
